From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:24:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] freedreno: advertise MESA_tile_raster_order on Xenos

Xenos samples from memory while it renders into EDRAM, and memory changes
only at resolves between draws, so a copy within one texture reads the
pre-draw contents in any raster order. glamor then scrolls and copies
overlapping areas without a temporary pixmap: scroll500 2160 -> 5520,
copywinwin500 2160 -> 5530.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QFJdrUq9L8NDS5PyGFCsG9
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_screen.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_screen.c
index e56634e..6d5309c 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_screen.c
@@ -404,6 +404,12 @@ fd_init_screen_caps(struct fd_screen *screen)
    caps->string_marker = true;
    caps->mixed_color_depth_bits = true;
    caps->texture_barrier = true;
+   /* Xenos samples textures from memory while it renders into EDRAM, and
+    * memory only changes at a resolve (between draws), so a draw that copies
+    * within one texture reads the pre-draw contents in any raster order.
+    * Advertising MESA_tile_raster_order lets glamor copy overlapping areas
+    * (scrolling) without a temporary pixmap. */
+   caps->tile_raster_order = is_xenos(screen);
    caps->invalidate_buffer = true;
    caps->glsl_tess_levels_as_inputs = true;
    caps->texture_mirror_clamp_to_edge = true;
